  "tier": "told-by-several",
  "plain": "In 1947, the story goes, a rancher named Mac Brazel found strange crash debris scattered over his land near Roswell, New Mexico, and it is told as the first famous UFO crash. A scientist named John Brandenburg, who credits Roswell veterans, says Brazel brought the wreckage into town and showed it to the sheriff, who told him to take it to the nearby air base. A researcher named Luigi Vendittelli adds that, besides the debris on the ranch, a pod holding beings crashed about two miles away, where hikers with children found it. A journalist named Michael Shellenberger asks whether one craft or two came down, possibly brought down by radar. A researcher of UFOs at nuclear sites named Robert Hastings says Roswell was then the world's only nuclear bomber base, and that Luis Elizondo calls it a real UFO crash in his new book, while Michels himself says he thinks what happened there was 'otherworldly'."
}
